## Why This Is Asked
Tests memory ownership across CGO, error handling, and concurrent access patterns. It pressures the candidate to manage allocation/deallocation boundaries and ensure thread-safety when crossing language borders.

## Key Concepts
- CGO memory ownership and free semantics
- Copying C buffers into Go safely
- Concurrency: independent CGO calls in parallel
- Error propagation from C to Go

## Code Example
